  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCS - British Council via Mercy Corps</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Planned Activities: The RAF top-up will expand the initially submitted market activities to include two additional outcomes:
o    Outcome 1: Household-level resilience via MPCA for persons with heightened security risks (protection referrals to MPCA). 
o    Outcome 2: Community resilience through GCTs for communal assets and training for local responder groups. CARE will be responsible for this outcome. 
o    Outcome 3: Market activities (including scaling activities that were already submitted in the initial proposal, but also expanding the scope slightly).
Overall implementation will align with the FCDO Financial Year, concluding on 31 March 2026. Start date as per the date of contract signature . MC expect signing one agreement over the full amount by end of October, which means overall 5 months of implementation for the full grant.</narrative>
  </description>
